🌺 Navratri Day 3 | Story and Vrat of Maa Chandraghanta 🙏

🙏 Jai Mata Di 🙏

The nine days of Navratri are dedicated to the nine divine forms of Goddess Durga. During this time, by worshipping the Mother, we try to purify our mind, body, and life. The third day of Navratri is devoted to Maa Chandraghanta.

Maa Chandraghanta gets her name from the moon (Chandra) and the bell (Ghanta) on her forehead. This form symbolizes courage, strength, and bravery. It is said that whenever devotees are attacked by evil or fear, Maa Chandraghanta protects them with her ten hands holding divine weapons.

According to a legend, when demons began tormenting the Earth and its devotees, Maa Chandraghanta appeared riding a lion. With her immense courage and power, she destroyed all evil. Seeing her divine form, all the gods and Lord Shiva were pleased. By her blessings, devotees’ hearts became fearless, and their lives were safeguarded.

Maa Chandraghanta wears white and yellow garments. She has ten hands, each holding weapons or symbols of blessings. Her mount is a lion, representing strength and valor.

Worshipping Maa Chandraghanta removes fear and negative energies. Her blessings instill self-confidence and guide devotees on the right path in life.

🍎 Special Prasad – sugar or mishri, fruits, milk, panchamrit, makhana, sabudana kheer, and coconut.
💡 Especially offering sugar/mishri and panchamrit is considered auspicious. Worshipping the Mother with a pure heart brings strength, sweetness, and positive energy into life.

🙏 Pray to the Mother —
Grant us courage, strength, and faith, and fill our lives with light and protection.

🌸 May Maa Chandraghanta bless you all 🌸
🙏 Jai Mata Di 🙏

