The nine days of Navratri are dedicated to the nine divine forms of Maa Durga. During these days, worshiping Maa helps us purify our mind, body, and life. The fourth day of Navratri is dedicated to Maa Kushmanda.

Kushmanda means – the beginning of creation. She is the energy that spreads life throughout the universe. Maa Kushmanda illuminates the entire cosmos with her divine smile and maintains balance in creation.

Maa Kushmanda has eight hands. Each hand holds a symbolic item:

🌸 In the first hand: Trishul – destroys evil and negative energies.

🗡️ In the second hand: Sword – symbolizes courage and strength.

🏹 In the third hand: Bow and Arrow – represents focus and determination.

🔱 In the fourth hand: Weapon – protects her devotees and righteousness.

🌺 In the fifth hand: Lotus – symbolizes peace and purity.

📿 In the sixth hand: Rosary – represents meditation and concentration.

💧 In the seventh hand: Water Pot – symbolizes life and energy.

✋ In the eighth hand: Blessing hand – gives happiness, peace, and strength to devotees.

Her vehicle is a lion, which represents courage and power.

Story:
When darkness and imbalance spread across the world, devotees were filled with fear and worry. Then Maa Kushmanda appeared with her eight hands and divine power. She used her weapons and blessings to destroy all evil. Her lotus and divine smile brought peace and confidence to the hearts of her devotees.

Worshiping Maa Kushmanda brings energy, health, and prosperity into life. Her blessings fill life with renewed enthusiasm and strength.

🙏 Pray to Maa –
Grant us energy, courage, and balance in life, and fill our lives with light.

🌸 May Maa Kushmanda bless you all 🌸
