🌸 Navratri Day 5 | Story of Maa Skandamata 🌸

🙏 Jai Mata Di 🙏

Navratri’s nine days are devoted to the nine divine forms of Goddess Durga. By worshipping the Mother during these days, we try to purify our mind, body, and life. The fifth day of Navratri is dedicated to Maa Skandamata.

Maa Skandamata is the mother of Lord Kartikeya (Skanda). Because of her maternal form, she is also called the Goddess of love, care, and protection. She blesses her devotees with wisdom, peace, and courage.

According to belief, when demons started spreading fear in the universe, the gods prayed for protection. Maa Skandamata appeared with her son Skanda in her lap. Her divine presence destroyed fear and restored balance in the world.

Maa Skandamata is seated on a lion and holds Lord Kartikeya in her lap. One hand carries a lotus, another grants blessings, and her divine weapons protect devotees from troubles. Her form teaches us that strength and compassion can exist together.

By worshipping Maa Skandamata, devotees receive calmness, confidence, and clarity in life. A mother’s grace removes sorrow and fills the heart with hope and devotion.

🙏 Prayer to Maa —
Bless us with wisdom, protection, and peace, and guide us on the right path.

🌸 Maa Skandamata, keep your blessings on everyone 🌸
